article_image_set_qa id=crop-060 attempt=1 pass=True score=88 duplicate_roles=[] reasons=["The three images successfully establish an editorial narrative flow for 'drip tape spacing' that is clearly distinct from a product-only focus. Image 1 offers a wide-scale 'establishment' view showing the layout of rows; Image 2 provides a technical 'field' view with visible drip tape and measurement elements; Image 3 shifts the focus to 'spacing' itself with a measuring tool. This progression fits the article's requirement for technical and agronomic evidence.", "Crop morphology aligns with the 'musk melon' topic: Image 2 clearly shows the large, broad leaves characteristic of cucurbit plants (melons/cucumbers), while Images 1 and 3 use the botanically neutral 'young vegetation' (seedling stage) permitted by the criteria to illustrate layout and spacing without misrepresenting the mature crop.", "The 'environment/background structure' criterion is met. The three images feature distinctly different visual compositions: a symmetrical wide-furrow perspective (1), a close-up side profile with agricultural infrastructure like posts (2), and a flat, low-angle top-down shot including a distant tractor (3). There are no duplicated camera angles or repetitive furrow compositions across the set.", "The technical narrative is strong and article-relevant. While no product is visible in the wide shot of Image 1, its inclusion of the 'AFP' branding watermark and its role in illustrating the final spacing layout maintains the editorial connection. There are zero people in any of the images."]
